<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arsaces I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 247 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arsaces I was the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arsacid-dynasty">Arsacid dynasty</a> and of the Parthian state, who seized the region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthia">Parthia</a> from Seleucid control around c. 247 BCE. Originally a leader of the nomadic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parni">Parni</a>, he established a kingdom that his successors expanded into a major empire. Later Parthian kings used Arsaces as a royal name in his honour.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arsaces-i.jpg" alt="Arsaces I" width="320" height="153" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Classical Numismatic Group; [1] · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_Arsaces_I_(1),_Nisa_mint.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
